{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#administrative-assistant-physician-assistant-sciences-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Physician Assistant Sciences- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Physician Assistant Sciences- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Application materials received before October 23, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University invites applications for a full-time Administrative Assistant I in the Department of Physician Assistant Sciences. The Administrative Assistant I is responsible to the chairperson and other PA Faculty for performing a variety of administrative support services. Execute day-to-day operations of the PA Department as well as directing student communications with faculty members. Serves as the department’s point of contact for other departments and offices on campus, to include admissions, financial aid, and the Center for Academic Success. Coordinates with the School of Health Sciences and Education office for resources and support. Minimum of a high school diploma with at least 1-2 years of secretarial, customer service and information training required. Associates degree is preferred. Good organizational, communication, proofreading and office management skills. Ability to work effectively with others to include prospective and current students, faculty and staff in support of program goals and operations is essential. Computer proficiency in word processing, spreadsheets and database systems required. Knowledge of Canvas Course Management Systems and Jenzabar preferred. Eligibility Requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Interested candidates should complete an online application , then submit a letter of application, references (names, mailing and email address, and telephone numbers), and current resume to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#assistant-director-financial-aid-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Financial Aid- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Financial Aid- Accepting Applications. Search Status : Application material received by October 23, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Open until filled. Saint Francis University invites applications for a full-time 12-month position as the Assistant Director, Financial Aid in the office of Financial Aid. The Assistant Director is responsible to the Director, Financial Aid to: Counsel families on aid application process while providing honest information about Saint Francis University with an emphasis on the value and importance of a liberal arts education. Overall knowledge of Jenzabar, updates, packaging requirements, processing, troubleshooting and reporting. Process financial aid applications with sensitivity to the diverse student population’ needs and attention to special needs of undergraduate, graduate, continuing education, and international students as well as students in the various minority groups represented on campus. Develop financial aid literacy programs and materials for undergraduate and graduate students. Package all students with special emphasis on special populations- GA, Remissions, etc. Title IV Distribution and reconciliation with DOE and Business Office. R2T4 withdrawal process. Bachelor’s degree is required; Master’s degree is strongly preferred. Significant and progressive experience in financial aid of at least 3 years. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Extensive experience and knowledge with the following software: COD, ELM Resources, FISAP, WS FTP, SQL, Jenzabar, Excel, SalesForce and PowerBuilder; Experience with PHEAA Needs Analysis, NCAA compliance experience preferred. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#coordinator-i-center-for-fine-arts-exercise-physiology-reviewing-applications-interviewing": {
      "title": "Coordinator I, Center for Fine Arts & Exercise Physiology- Reviewing Applications/Interviewing",
      "description": "Coordinator I, Center for Fine Arts & Exercise Physiology- Reviewing Applications/Interviewing. Search Status : Application material received by October 2, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University invites applications for a full-time position Coordinator I in the Center for Fine Arts and the Department of Exercise Physiology. The Coordinator I provides professional, confidential administrative and academic support for the Center for Fine Arts and Exercise Physiology. This position is split between the Center for Fine Arts and Exercise Physiology. The position supports office operations, departmental records, budgets, communication, recruitment activities, meetings, events, student workers, and other duties as assigned. The position requires on-site work in both areas and may require occasional irregular hours to support events, performances, visits, or departmental activities. Associate degree or at least 1-3 years of secretarial/administrative experience is required. At least two years of related higher education experience is preferred. Proficient in grammar, spelling, and proofreading skills; accurate data entry skills; proficient skills in Microsoft Suites and Google suite. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, strong problem solving skills, strong organizational and office management skills, and the ability to work independently and with limited supervision on a wide range of program tasks. Knowledge of Canvas Learning Management System, Jenzabar, Salesforce, Cognos, or similar systems preferred. Knowledge of web page authoring, social media platforms, or related software preferred. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#general-carpenter-drywaller-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "General Carpenter/Drywaller- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "General Carpenter/Drywaller- Accepting Applications. Search Status : Application material received by October 23 , 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University invites applications for a General Carpenter/Drywaller position in the department of Physical Plant. The General Carpenter/Drywaller is directly responsible to the General Trades Supervisor for performing a variety of carpentry tasks aside other members of the physical plant group. Assume lead role for projects involving wall construction, framing, drywall, drywall finishing, and painting. High school graduate with vocational/technical training in general carpentry or related areas. Knowledge of carpentry, painting, roofing, masonry, flooring and associated tools. Knowledge of blueprint reading as it pertains to carpentry trade. Basic mathematical skills are necessary. Minimum of two years of commercial or residential construction experience in general carpentry field is required. Experience with drywalling and finishing is highly preferred. Must have valid driver's license. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#general-carpenter-flooring-specialist-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "General Carpenter/Flooring Specialist- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "General Carpenter/Flooring Specialist- Accepting Applications. Search Status : Application material received by October 23, 2026 will receive primary consideration. S aint Francis University invites applications for a General Carpenter/Flooring Specialist position in the department of Physical Plant. The General Carpenter/Flooring Specialist is directly responsible to the General Trades Supervisor for performing a variety of carpentry tasks aside other members of the physical plant group. Assume lead role for projects involving new carpeting, Luxury Vinyl Tile (LVT), Vinyl Composition Tile (VCT), or any other flooring material. High school graduate with vocational/technical training in general carpentry or related areas. Knowledge of carpentry, painting, roofing, masonry, flooring and associated tools. Knowledge of blueprint reading as it pertains to carpentry trade. Basic mathematical skills are necessary. Minimum of two years of commercial or residential construction experience in general carpentry field is required. Experience installing commercial flooring is highly preferred. Must have valid driver's license. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#graduate-assistants-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistants - Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Graduate Assistants - Accepting Applications. Graduate Assistantships are offered at Saint Francis University in a variety of academic and administrative departments throughout campus. Current Open Positions: Graduate Assistant, Men's & Women's Track & Field Graduate Assistant, Men's & Women's Golf Graduate Assistant, Center for Academic Success Graduate Assistant, Division of Professional Studies Requirements: Bachelor's degree required Acceptance to one of the University's graduate programs as a full-time student Each department may have additional requirements (ex. athletics- coaching/playing experience) Once hired, completion of a Graduate Assistant contract through Academic Affairs- terms to be determined between the sponsoring department and the Graduate Assistant. If hired in an athletic coaching position another contract is issued from Human Resources. Tuition Remission: Graduate assistants are eligible for full tuition remission for up to 9 credits per semester. Summer varies according to each department. Positions as a coach within Athletics may offer a stipend in addition to tuition remission Fees, books and additional credits are the responsibility of the Graduate Assistant Questions: For questions about the Graduate Assistant, Track & Field please contact Doug Hoover For questions about the Graduate Assistant, Golf please contact Jonathan Kulas. For questions about the Graduate Assistant, Academic Success please contact Sandra Rea. For questions about the Graduate Assistant, Division of Professional Studies please contact Leslie Himes. For questions about the program, please contact: careerservices@francis.edu . Applying for Current or Future GA Positions: Complete a SFU employment application Complete a Graduate Assistant Addendum Send a letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to positions@francis.edu and careerservices@francis.edu"
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#marketing-campaign-specialist-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Marketing Campaign Specialist- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Marketing Campaign Specialist- Accepting Applications. Search Status : Application material received by October 26, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Open until filled. Saint Francis University invites applications for a full-time 12-month position as Marketing Campaign Specialist in the Department of University Communications & Marketing. The Marketing Campaign Specialist supports the planning, coordination, and execution of marketing initiatives that advance Saint Francis University’s enrollment, academic programs, and institutional priorities. As a member of University Communications & Marketing, the Marketing Campaign Specialist coordinates campaigns and projects across digital, print, web, email, social media, and advertising; works with campus partners to gather information and create assets; supports agency and vendor relationships; and assists with tracking campaign schedules, budgets, and results. Bachelor’s degree is required with one to three years of experience in marketing, communications, advertising, social media, project coordination, or a related area preferred. Strong organization, dependability, and attention to detail. Strong writing skills and sound judgment about audience and tone. Ability to build effective working relationships across an organization. Initiative in identifying questions, missing information, and next steps. Comfortable learning new software, systems, and digital marketing tools. Ability to work independently on assigned responsibilities while recognizing when guidance or approval is needed. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#assistant-director-athletic-communication-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Athletic Communication- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Athletic Communication- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Application material received by October 16, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University, a Division III member of the Presidents’ Athletic Conference, invites applications for a full time Assistant Director, Athletic Communications. The Assistant Director is responsible for assisting with publicizing the 21-sport Division III intercollegiate athletic programs at Saint Francis University and all aspects of the Saint Francis Athletics program, including but not limited to, game day include operation of live statistics, posting to social media, writing game recaps, and managing broadcast operations and student workers. The Assistant Director will be the primary media contact for select sports. The successful candidate must have a commitment to and responsibility for adhering to all rules and regulations of Saint Francis University, the PAC, and the NCAA. In addition, the candidate must understand and actively support the mission of the Department of Athletics and Saint Francis University. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree is preferred. Excellent writing, computer, organization, and communication skills are necessary. At least two years of experience in sports information/athletic communications professional level preferred. Experience with desktop publishing (InDesign), graphics software (Photoshop, Illustrator), and video editing. Knowledge of live statistical and game-scoring software platforms (Stat Crew and NCAA live stats) for football, basketball, volleyball, and soccer is preferred. Experience with graphic design and video editing is also recommended. Apply on line , then submit a letter of application, resume and names and addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#graduate-assistant-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant- Accepting Applications. Saint Francis University invites applications for the following Graduate Assistant positions in the Athletic Department: Graduate Assistant- Creative Video and Athletic Broadcasting Athletic Communications Graduate Assistant- Athletic Video Production Graduate Assistant- Men's & Women's Golf Saint Francis University, is a member of the NCAA Division III competing in the Presidents' Athletic Conference. The candidates must have a commitment to adhering to all rules and regulations of Saint Francis University, Presidents' Athletic Conference and the NCAA. In addition, the candidates must understand and actively support the mission of the Department of Athletics and Saint Francis University. Bachelor's degree required. Intercollegiate competitive or coaching experience required for coaching positions. Excellent oral, written and interpersonal skills are essential. Compensation for the position is tuition remission in a Saint Francis University Master's degree program, plus a stipend if coaching. The successful candidate must apply and be admitted to a Saint Francis University's masters program in order to qualify for the positions. Questions regarding specific GA positions please contact one of the following: Questions concerning GA positions in Athletic Communications should be directed to Chris Miller ( CMiller@francis.edu ), Assistant Director of Athletics for Marketing, Promotions and Communications Questions concerning GA positions with Golf should be directed to Jonathan Kulas ( JKulas@francis.edu ), Head Coach, Men's & Women's Golf General Questions can be directed to Lisa Swope ( LSwope@francis.edu ) Senior Associate AD for Athletic Operations/SWA. Apply online and then submit a letter of application, resume, and names, addresses, and phone numbers of references to positions@francis.edu . Applications accepted until the position is filled. Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#faculty-biology-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Faculty, Biology- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Faculty, Biology- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Application Material received by November 16 , 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in the Biology department to begin August 2027. Teaching responsibilities will include cell and molecular biology courses in support of our biology major. Specific courses may include genetics, biochemistry, cell and molecular biology, immunology, courses within the candidate’s area of expertise, and other needs within the department such as non-majors human heredity. The candidate must sustain an active research agenda that involves undergraduate students. Additional responsibilities include undergraduate advising and other departmental/university service. A terminal degree in Biology or a related discipline is required at the time the position starts (ABD applicants will be considered). The candidate must demonstrate aptitude and zeal for teaching; experience as a primary course instructor in a college setting is desirable. Candidates must provide evidence of potential and drive to pursue undergraduate research that is viable at a small institution. Saint Francis University is the oldest Catholic-Franciscan College in the United States. We are a predominantly undergraduate institution in Loretto, PA, which is located in Central Pennsylvania two hours east of Pittsburgh and three hours from Washington, D.C. The University enrolls 1875 students as of Fall 2025 of which ~1,500 are undergraduates. The Biology department includes 12 full-time faculty and ~115 majors. Our department's student body is a mix of general biology, pre-medicine, marine biology, and aquarium & zoo science students, along with smaller numbers of students in other specialties. We are housed in the Science Center, a 70,000-square foot facility, with modern teaching classrooms and labs, along with dedicated research space including a cell culture facility. Graduates of our programs pursue graduate and professional school at institutions across the country. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. To apply: Complete an application , then email cover letter, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, undergraduate research plan, unofficial transcripts, and a list of three professional references to: positions@francis.edu. Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, with video interviews planned for the week of November 30th. Three letters of recommendation will be requested prior to invitations for on-campus interviews. Salary range information is available to applicants upon request. Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#faculty-chemistry-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Faculty, Chemistry- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Faculty, Chemistry- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Application material received by October 30, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University Department of Chemistry invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in physical chemistry starting August 2027. Primary duties include teaching courses in physical chemistry (including laboratories), general chemistry (including laboratories), chemistry for health science students (general, organic, and biochemistry), and some laboratory preparation/equipment maintenance. Other duties include but are not limited to mentoring research projects, advising students, and continued professional development. The successful candidate must have a PhD in Chemistry, a commitment to excellence in chemical education in the classroom and in the research laboratory, and preferably post-doctoral research experience. This new faculty member will join a vibrant ACS approved chemistry program and research community with opportunities for collaboration across campus and local industry. Dedicated research space is available in the 78,000-sf. science center. Review of applications will begin in late October with phone and on-campus interviews planned for early November through December. Saint Francis University is a liberal arts institution, located in Loretto, PA about a 30-minute drive from Altoona, PA and Johnstown, PA. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Apply online , then submit a letter of application, Curriculum Vitae, teaching philosophy, research statement, unofficial transcripts, and names, addresses, and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu . Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#faculty-physical-therapy-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Faculty, Physical Therapy- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Faculty, Physical Therapy- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Review of application material will begin August 17, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Saint Francis University in Loretto, Pennsylvania invites applications for a full-time,12-month faculty position in their entry-level Doctor of Physical Therapy program. Teaching load will be developed in the candidate’s area(s) of expertise. Preference will be given to candidates with interest in Cardiopulmonary, Orthopedics, or other areas of clinical specialization. This position includes: teaching in the professional curriculum as assigned; service on University, School of Health Sciences and Education, and Department committees as appointed; participation in departmental activities including accreditation maintenance, curriculum development and evaluation, student research mentorship, student advisement, professional development activities, and community outreach; participation in the University’s Core Curriculum Program; and other duties as assigned. The successful candidate will engage in research, which may be through the Human Performance Laboratory in the DiSepio Institute for Rural Health and Wellness. Faculty rank and tenure track eligibility will be commensurate with the candidate’s experience and qualifications. Requirements for candidacy include a doctoral degree in Physical Therapy (DPT), unencumbered current licensure in Pennsylvania or eligibility, and a minimum 3-5 years of clinical experience. Preferred qualifications include a terminal academic degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, or equivalent) or degree in progress; board certified clinical specialization recognized by ABPTS; prior teaching or lecture experience; APTA membership. Candidates who do not possess a terminal academic degree may be required to agree to obtain such as a condition of hire. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Apply online , and then submit letter of application; Curriculum Vitae; unofficial transcripts; and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#financial-aid-counselor-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor- Accepting Applications. Search Status : Application material received by November 13, 2026 will receive primary consideration Saint Francis University invites applications for a full-time 12-month position as a Financial Aid Counselor in the Department of Financial Aid. The Financial Aid Counselor is responsible to: Counsel families on aid application process while providing honest information about Saint Francis University with an emphasis on the value and importance of a liberal arts education. Process financial aid applications with sensitivity to the diverse student populations’ needs and attention to special needs of undergraduate, graduate, continuing education, and international students as well as students in the various minority groups represented on campus. Manage student federal and campus-based employment program and oversee the work-study students within the Financial Aid Office. Develop financial aid debt management program and materials for undergraduate and graduate students. Package all graduate students with special emphasis on Master populations as well as Adult Degree and Continuing Studies student populations. Complete and manage consortium agreements for both Master and Undergraduate populations. Bachelor’s degree is preferred. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Experience and knowledge with the following software: COD, ELM Resources, WS FTP, SQL, Jenzabar, Excel, PowerBuilder. Experience with PHEAA Needs Analysis preferred, but not required. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application, then submit letter of application, resume, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#assistant-director-athletic-communication-reviewing-interviewing": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Athletic Communication- Reviewing/Interviewing",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Athletic Communication- Reviewing/Interviewing. Search Status: Application material received by October 16, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University, a Division III member of the Presidents’ Athletic Conference, invites applications for a full time Assistant Director, Athletic Communications. The Assistant Director is responsible for assisting with publicizing the 21-sport Division III intercollegiate athletic programs at Saint Francis University and all aspects of the Saint Francis Athletics program, including but not limited to, game day include operation of live statistics, posting to social media, writing game recaps, and managing broadcast operations and student workers. The Assistant Director will be the primary media contact for select sports. The successful candidate must have a commitment to and responsibility for adhering to all rules and regulations of Saint Francis University, the PAC, and the NCAA. In addition, the candidate must understand and actively support the mission of the Department of Athletics and Saint Francis University. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree is preferred. Excellent writing, computer, organization, and communication skills are necessary. At least two years of experience in sports information/athletic communications professional level preferred. Experience with desktop publishing (InDesign), graphics software (Photoshop, Illustrator), and video editing. Knowledge of live statistical and game-scoring software platforms (Stat Crew and NCAA live stats) for football, basketball, volleyball, and soccer is preferred. Experience with graphic design and video editing is also recommended. Apply on line , then submit a letter of application, resume and names and addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    },
    "https://www.francis.edu/about-us/employment#adjuncts-philosophy-accepting-applications": {
      "title": "Adjuncts, Philosophy- Accepting Applications",
      "description": "Adjuncts, Philosophy- Accepting Applications. Search Status: Application material received by November 6, 2026 will receive primary consideration. Saint Francis University invites applications for adjuncts to teach in our Department of Theology & Philosophy. Adjuncts would be asked to teach up to three sections of PHIL105: Intro to Philosophy, beginning in Spring 2027. We anticipate a continuing need for these sections through Spring 2028, subject to enrollment. This course is a foundational element of our undergraduate core curriculum and is taken by most students in their freshman year. Candidates must hold at least a master’s degree in philosophy and embrace the Catholic vision of university education and philosophy expressed in Pope St. John Paul’s II’s Ex Corde Ecclesiae and Fides et Ratio , respectively. Preference will be given to applicants who can teach on campus on Tuesdays & Thursdays, but those who require hybrid or fully online formats will also be considered. Eligibility requirement: Candidates must have current authorization to work in the United States. We are unable to provide visa sponsorship or assist with work authorization. Complete an online application , then submit letter of application, CV, unofficial transcript, a sample syllabus for PHIL 105, and names, addresses and phone numbers of three references to: positions@francis.edu Saint Francis University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-472-3264 or positions@francis.edu ."
    }
  },
